  "body": "### Summary\nAs ezzz or a parity checker, I want a legacy pointer to land on the cited symbol, and comments to say what is true today, so that the pointers of AGENTS §4 stay a starting point. About 30 pointers were spot-checked in this review; one is wrong, and nothing in CI would catch the next one.\n\n### Evidence (`7a61018f`)\n- Wrong pointer: `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/AppIconSettingsView.swift:4`: \"(icon Picker, lines 360-365, `applyIconSelection` 213-224) @ 87fe0d1c\". At `87fe0d1c`, `git show 87fe0d1c:HFRswift/Swift/AppSettingsView.swift` has `applyIconSelection` at line 221 and `Picker(\"Icône\"` at 411; 213 and 360 are the `2440d79` lines (the sha was moved without the lines, which AGENTS §2 warns against).\n- Stale: `App/SwiftHFR/Common/HapticFeedback.swift:5` \"no call site exists yet\" and `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicListView.swift:9` \"no haptics caller yet\": callers exist (`Settings/Seasons/NoelCrossingModel.swift:177`, `Reader/ReaderPageEnd.swift:55`).\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/PagerToolbar.swift:3-5`: the third line of the `//` port comment starts with `///`, so the type's doc comment begins mid-sentence.\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderView.swift:152`: \"no composer in Messages\" (false since LOT-128; see the linked-MP finding of #775).\n- Stale wording: `MessageMenuContext.isQuoteSelectionEnabled` \"LOT-086 owns it, false until then\", `LinkActionHandler` \"the only action implemented by LOT-087 itself\" (`Reader/Actions/MessageMenuAction.swift`, `MessageActionRegistry.swift`).\n- `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRModels/MPStorage/MPStorageMerge.swift:6-7`: the header says other entries come from `theirs` \"unless this app changed them\", but `merge` never reads the other entries of `ours` (`:37-38`).\n- `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRParsing/HFRParsing.swift:12`: `documentTitle`, \"replaced by real parsers in Phase 3\", is still public and used only by `EngineInfo` tests.\n\n### Fix\nCorrect the comments (icon pointer: 221-232 and 411-416 @ `87fe0d1c`, to re-read). Class fix: `tooling/docs/check_legacy_pointers.py`, which for each `<Symbol> … :a-b @ <sha>` in `App/` checks the named symbol appears in the cited range of `git show <sha>:<path>`, run in the Docs consistency job.\n\n### Test\nThe checker's own test on the `AppIconSettingsView` line: red today.\n\nRework model: Haiku 5.5, reviewed by Opus 5.5.\n\nFound by #775 (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2). Reviewed at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`; read from the code, not run on a device unless stated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
