   "body": "/claim cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet\n\nPlan (one PR, comments only, no behaviour change):\n- Correct each comment of the issue: the `AppIconSettingsView.swift` pointer re-read at `87fe0d1c` (`git show 87fe0d1c:HFRswift/Swift/AppSettingsView.swift`), the two stale \"no haptics caller yet\" notes, the `PagerToolbar.swift` port comment split from its doc comment, `TopicReaderView.swift:152`, the LOT-086/LOT-087 wording in `MessageMenuAction.swift` / `MessageActionRegistry.swift`, the `MPStorageMerge.swift` header, the `HFRParsing.swift` Phase 3 note; each re-verified against the code before editing.\n- The pointer checker (`tooling/docs/check_legacy_pointers.py` in the Docs consistency job) is the class fix; as asked by cloud/orch it goes to a follow-up issue unless trivial (it is not: it needs a parser for the pointer formats and a CI step), so this PR is `Refs`-free only if that issue is opened first; I open it and link it here.\n- Overlap checked with the open PRs (#1239, #1246, #1247, #1250, #1251, #1141, #1131, #1222, #1223, #1227): #1247 already rewrites the `HapticFeedback.swift` header note, so that item is checked against `dev-swift` at branch time.\n- Draft PR with `compile-check` (comments cannot break the build, but a doc-comment mistake can: `///` vs `//`), Opus review, ready line on #893.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
